id: pm-gh1704
title: "GH-1704: secret guard flags short credential values only under password keys; api_key, client_secret, token and *_TOKEN/*_SECRET keys pass"
description: "GH-1704 (filed 2026-11-11). On 2026.11.11 the secret guard flags a short credential value under password and passphrase keys only. A 17-character random value under api_key, client_secret, token, passwd, db_password, private_key, GITHUB_TOKEN, NPM_TOKEN or AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY passes scanMutationSecrets and the default advise write path in the key: v, key=v and JSON spellings. The high_entropy_assignment rule covers token, secret, password, passwd and api_key only from 24 characters with entropy 3.5, and covers neither client_secret nor compound keys such as db_password. Agents paste env excerpts, CI logs and pasted configs into comments and descriptions, and that is exactly the shape that leaks. Packages cannot rely on the SDK scanner, so pm-memory keeps its own parser. Proposal from the issue: one credential-key rule that reuses the pm-gh1699 KEY plus VALUE composition, the structured JSON, Python-dict and XML pass, an 8-character minimum, whitespace-free values and the placeholder exclusions, with a must-allow corpus (token_budget, max_tokens, token_count, placeholders, prose, localization labels)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"gh:1704",sdk,secret-guard,security
created_at: "2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-12T14:21:15.825Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-12T08:56:29.386Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-12T08:56:29.386Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "One credential-key rule flags 8+ character whitespace-free non-placeholder values under secret, token, api key, private key, access key, client secret, passwd, pwd and compound *_password/*_secret/*_token/*_api_key/*_private_key keys in any case, in key: v, key=v, JSON, Python-dict and XML spellings; A must-allow corpus stays clean: token_budget, max_tokens, output_token_budget, numeric token counts, placeholders, prose and localization labels; The SDK scanMutationSecrets and the CLI advise path agree on the corpus"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "New mutation-only secret rule credential_key_assignment in src/core/shared/secret-rules.ts. It covers keys whose last word names a credential (secret, token, api/secret/private/access key, client secret, passwd, pwd) and underscore compounds such as DB_PASSWORD, aws_secret_access_key and GITHUB_TOKEN, in key: v, key=v, JSON, Python-dict and XML-element spellings through the GH-1699 structured pass. Values need 8 or more whitespace-free characters and entropy of at least 3 bits per character, and must not be placeholders (<...>, ${...}, $(...), $VAR, %VAR%, [scrubbed]), paths, dotted member paths or calls. Plain and hyphenated password keys stay with password_assignment, so each value is reported once. The repository scan is unchanged because the rule is mutation-only."
expected_result: Every row of the GH-1704 table flags in all three spellings plus XML; the must-allow corpus stays clean
actual_result: "secret-policy-parity: 17 keys x 3 spellings plus XML flag credential_key_assignment; 19 must-allow cases stay clean; block mode refuses; 422 secret-guard tests pass and every changed line is covered"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1699,related,"2026-11-12T05:13:22.718Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T09:36:14.397Z","harness:claude-code","Pre-push Codex review (three P2s), fixed before the PR opened. (1) Element content went through the generic length check, so <token>********</token> and <secret>[scrubbed]</secret> were flagged; the spelling now declares elementValue and element content is judged by the value grammar and entropy predicate. (2) A quoted value matched its first word, so client_secret: \"Configure this in the settings page\" and {\"token\":\"authentication failed\"} were flagged; a quoted value must now be whitespace-free up to its closing quote, and letters-only words are excluded. (3) A word boundary after each hyphen let the compound-key prefix restart inside one identifier, which is quadratic on a hyphen run; a lookbehind now starts a key only at the beginning of an identifier and still allows --token=. The credential rule scans 32 KB hyphen runs in under 20 ms. The remaining second of cost on that input belongs to the pre-existing user_at_private_host rule, filed as pm-3627y1.\n"
  "2026-11-12T09:54:06.403Z","harness:claude-code","Pre-push Codex review round 2 (P2), fixed before the PR opened: element content matched the value grammar on a prefix, so <client_secret>not-configured in this environment</client_secret> was flagged and blocked in block mode, while the equivalent quoted JSON value stayed clean. The whole trimmed element body must now be one value. The case is in the must-allow corpus.\n"
  "2026-11-12T10:48:34.319Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 review (Greptile, CodeRabbit), fixed in this PR. (1) Greptile: the credential value class left out ?, : and |, so client_secret: \"q7!A?9#z\" passed in every spelling; they now count as value characters, and URL values are excluded so token: https://… stays clean.\n"
  "2026-11-12T11:08:35.044Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 review round 2 (Codex, Greptile), fixed in this PR. Widening the value class with ? and | made pasted code count as a credential: token=process.env.API_KEY||\"\", api_key=process.env.API_KEY??\"\", token = options?.token ?? fallback and token = config.auth?.token. ? : | now count only inside a quoted value or an element body, which is judged as a quoted literal. Unquoted values keep the code-safe alphabet, and the four expressions are in the must-allow corpus.\n"
  "2026-11-12T11:23:15.711Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 review round 3 (Codex, Greptile), fixed in this PR. Narrowing the member-path exclusion to the unquoted alphabet also applied it inside quoted values, so \"a1.B2c?D3\" and \"svc.app.region:secretX09Ab\" passed in plain, JSON, array and XML form. The member-path and call exclusions are now quote-aware: unquoted, they use the code-safe boundary; quoted (and element bodies), a value is a member path only when the whole literal is one (\"process.env.GITHUB_TOKEN\"). Both secrets and the quoted member path are in the spec.\n"
  "2026-11-12T11:42:03.190Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 Codex review round 4, fixed in this PR. (1) The letters-only exclusion still used the wide boundary for unquoted values, so const token = configuration?.token; was flagged: the exclusion missed because of ?, and the unquoted capture stopped there. The exclusion is now quote-aware like the member-path one. (2) Key-file references such as {\"private_key\":\"certs/client.key\"} and C:/ProgramData/keys/client.pem were flagged. Unprefixed relative paths ending in an extension and Windows drive paths are now excluded. All four cases are in the must-allow corpus.\n"
  "2026-11-12T11:50:22.388Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 CodeRabbit (Minor), fixed in this PR: unquoted prose such as client_secret: not-configured in this environment matched its first hyphenated word. Letters-and-hyphens-only values are now excluded in both contexts, and both cases are in the must-allow corpus.\n"
  "2026-11-12T12:20:09.111Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 Codex review on 59bd3aafb (two P2 false positives in block mode), fixed in this PR. The rule now declares a case-sensitive rejectValue for CONSTANT_CASE references (const token = DEFAULT_TOKEN;) and SSH key-file names (keys/id_ed25519, .ssh/id_rsa); acceptsSecretMatch applies it before entropy. A lowercase provider key such as sk_live_... still flags. Further false-positive shapes go to the measured corpus in pm-1l85at rather than another review round.\n"
  "2026-11-12T12:32:27.225Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 final Codex round (P2 escape), fixed in this PR. The CONSTANT_CASE exemption also accepted digits, so a real uppercase credential such as {\"api_key\":\"ZQ8VN3K_LMP0WXY7AB\"} escaped detection. It now accepts only letters and underscores (DEFAULT_TOKEN, API_KEY_FROM_ENV); an uppercase literal containing digits flags in JSON and env form.\n"
  "2026-11-12T12:46:58.942Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 final Codex round 2 (two P2 escapes), fixed in this PR. (1) A digit-free uppercase literal such as ZQVNKR_LMPWXYAB still matched the CONSTANT_CASE exemption, because no value-only rule can tell a constant from a literal. The exemption is now contextual: only an unquoted CONSTANT_CASE name that ends a statement (= DEFAULT_TOKEN;) counts as a reference. Quoted, JSON, XML and env values always count. (2) CLIENT_SECRET=q7!A?9#z stopped at the question mark. Unquoted values directly after = now use the wide alphabet, and the member-path and word exclusions still catch code such as token=process.env.API_KEY||\"\".\n"
  "2026-11-12T13:06:18.199Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 final Codex round 3. Fixed: (1) The statement-constant exclusion inherited the detector's case-insensitive flag, so the mixed-case literal Zqvnkr_LmPwxyAb; escaped. It is now a declared, case-sensitive post-match check (rejectStatementReference), applied only to an unquoted value whose statement a semicolon ends. Declined with reason: (2) unquoted env values such as CLIENT_SECRET=AbCd?7x9, whose segment before ? is letters-only or a dotted path. Judging those exclusions with the wide alphabet re-flags code such as token=options?.token, a false positive an earlier round asked to fix, and the case-insensitive rule cannot tell the two apart. Quoted, JSON and XML forms are detected, and the residual is recorded for the measured corpus in pm-1l85at.\n"
  "2026-11-12T13:29:57.734Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 CodeRabbit (Minor), fixed in this PR: const token = DEFAULT_TOKEN ; (space before the semicolon) was flagged; the statement-reference check accepts horizontal whitespace before the semicolon. Codex (P2 escape), fixed: CLIENT_SECRET=\"ZQVNKR_LMPWXYAB;\" was exempted because the quote check looked at the start of the whole match; it now looks at the character before the captured value.\n"
  "2026-11-12T13:51:59.285Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 Codex (P2 escape), fixed in this PR: a quoted credential containing ;, comma or ( (\"q7!A;9#z\") stopped short of eight characters. A quoted value or element body is now captured whole up to its closing quote; the unquoted code-safe alphabet is unchanged.\n"
  "2026-11-12T14:07:06.717Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 Codex (two P2 escapes), fixed in this PR. Once quoted values were captured whole, the letters-only exclusion still rejected the prefix before a semicolon (\"ZqvnKr;LmP0wXy7Ab\"), and an apostrophe inside a double-quoted value ended the capture. The quoted word, member-path and key-file exclusions now require the whole literal up to its matching quote, and the capture ends only at the quote that opened it. Both shapes are covered for client_secret JSON and a DB_PASSWORD element.\n"
  "2026-11-12T14:21:15.824Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1712 CodeRabbit (Major) and Codex, fixed in this PR: an element body containing a double quote (<client_secret>q7!A\"9#z</client_secret>) ended the synthetic quoted literal early and escaped. The body's own double quotes are now neutralized before it is judged as one value. Declined with reason (CodeRabbit Minor): unquoted values after a colon or a spaced equals sign containing ? : |, such as client_secret: q7!A?9#z. In those positions such punctuation reads as code ({ token: options?.token }), the same trade-off as before. Quoted, JSON, XML and direct env (KEY=value) forms are detected.\n"
